00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:39,520
I talked, you know, just recently a few weeks ago to a person who is a founder of a pretty big tech company and he said we He said, We need some sort of quick formation resource.

255
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:56,720
He basically said that he himself was starting to read Russian literature, the classics of Russian literature, to try to get a better understanding of something that he had never really thought about in his entire life, despite the fact that he was an extremely technologically or extremely successful person in terms of technology.

256
00:36:57,120 --> 00:37:02,640
He had not thought about the formation side of things because it was not part of the technical education that he received.

257
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:12,480
Something that's good about Catholic education is that it's very hard to get out of a Catholic school, at least a good Catholic university, without having a lot of exposure to the humanities in various senses.

