00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:19,440
And so we hopefully generate better, more well rounded engineers than secular universities are.

259
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:24,880
But this sort of need for resources is something that we can think about.

260
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:29,520
What would we want the folks in the tech industry to know if we could share anything with them?

261
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:35,360
And certainly there are things, you know, it would be great if we could frame this as Catholicly as possible.

262
00:37:35,600 --> 00:37:41,520
But on the other hand, they're not going to accept something if it comes from a Catholic perspective because they're kind of allergic to that by nature.

263
00:37:42,080 --> 00:37:55,760
So we have to figure out how to secularize this message in a way that makes it digestible and yet at the same time., it is not so watered down that they don't get anything from it that's actually going to help, you know, fix the problems of the world.

264
00:37:56,720 --> 00:37:58,720
So we have this translation issue going on also.

265
00:37:58,960 --> 00:38:12,560
Not only are there a bunch of differences in definitions, there's also differences in terms of how we can actually, can we actually translate things from one language to another or is it just impossible without that next step of conversion?

