00:46:05,120 --> 00:46:05,200
Okay.

309
00:46:05,760 --> 00:46:06,880
I read it and I gave feedback.

310
00:46:07,360 --> 00:46:08,240
You didn't get to sign it.

311
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:09,920
I didn't sign it.

312
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:11,360
I was just one of the outside readers.

313
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:12,960
But I'm not sure.

314
00:46:12,960 --> 00:46:20,640
But what I will say is that even the people producing this technology do not understand how it operates fundamentally.

315
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:24,480
And this is something that we as outsiders all need to recognize, right?

316
00:46:24,720 --> 00:46:30,960
It's like usually when people create a technology, they're like, Hey, it's my phone, it's a smartphone, I know how it operates, right?

317
00:46:31,600 --> 00:46:38,080
There are chips and circuits and receivers and all those sorts of things that are comprehensible.

318
00:46:39,440 --> 00:46:45,200
The way that the neural network is put together is as an organic outgrowth of an algorithm interacting with data.

319
00:46:45,840 --> 00:46:48,560
And so when it is exposed to enormous amounts of work.

320
00:46:48,720 --> 00:46:58,640
of words, it starts drawing the statistical patterns of inference, not just between individual words, but up to the sentence level, the paragraph level, whole pages of connections.

321
00:46:59,360 --> 00:47:08,160
And so it's really operating in these large language models, it's operating in a way which is getting to be, in some sense, I would say superhuman.

322
00:47:08,640 --> 00:47:10,400
And so it's already difficult to understand.

323
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:15,120
When I say superhuman, I don't necessarily mean it's smarter than we are, quote, unquote, or more intelligent.

324
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:18,160
It's operating in a way that's just very difficult to understand.

325
00:47:18,400 --> 00:47:22,640
And it's drawing connections that are not necessarily connections that humans normally draw.

326
00:47:23,360 --> 00:47:28,800
And when you are exposed to it a technology like this and you're like, hey, let's try to control this thing we don't understand.

327
00:47:29,600 --> 00:47:30,000
Guess what?

328
00:47:30,240 --> 00:47:30,960
It doesn't really work.

329
00:47:31,440 --> 00:47:37,360
I mean, this is this is this goes back to, you know, old testament type stuff when we're dealing with idolatry.

